From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:29:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 193/342] dwc2: high speed isochronous IN, one packet a
 microframe (M45, testing)

A third isochronous stream (channel 4) for high speed endpoints, with
256 KiB slots: a packet descriptor per microframe, up to wMaxPacketSize
times the transactions per microframe (HCCHAR.MC, PKTCNT, a DATA0, DATA1
or DATA2 start for 1, 2 or 3). Each packet is armed from the halt of the
one before for the next microframe (ODDFRM); microframes the chain
misses, overruns, incomplete and short packets go into the stop summary.
For now only IN endpoints with bInterval 1 (a webcam's video). Still with
debug output for the C920 tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
